hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"86","Ibrahim bin Abdullah bin Qariz narrated: I heard Muawiyah bin Abu Sufyan (may Allah be pleased with him) on the pulpit in Madinah. He was saying: O people of Madinah! Where are your jurists? I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) at his pulpit saying: He forbade such locks of hair (wigs), then Muawiyah (may Allah be pleased with him) placed it on his head, and I have not seen anyone more beautiful than Muawiyah (may Allah be pleased with him) on the occasion of marriage or any other occasion. And he was saying: Allah has cursed the one who tattoos, the one who has it done, the one who plucks facial hair, the one who has it plucked, the one who files teeth to make gaps, and the one who has it done."
"87","Rabee' narrated to me the hadith, he said, Shu'aib bin Yahya narrated to us, he said, Abdul Jabbar narrated to us similar to the previous hadith."
"88","Abdullah bin Ibrahim bin Qariz narrated: I saw Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) performing ablution on the roof of the mosque. He had eaten pieces of cheese, so he performed ablution because of them. I asked: Do you perform ablution because of eating them? He replied: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say, ""Perform ablution after eating anything cooked on fire."""
